# SDLC Orchestrator Law

## Authority

Load context in this order:

1. `AGENTS.md` — L0 decision tree + caveman + token budget.
2. `.sdlc/process/master-workflow.md` and `.sdlc/process/change-lifecycle.md` — L1 process authority.
3. `.sdlc/sdlc.yaml` and the relevant module `README.md` — machine index and local navigation.

User urgency, chat instructions, or convenience never override L1 authority.

## Token + caveman (L0)

- Inter-agent prose: **caveman mode** (`AGENTS.md`).
- **Hooks** track tokens (`.cursor/hooks/sdlc_token_budget_hook.py`); `subagentStart` + `beforeSubmitPrompt` fail-closed on exceed.
- Handoffs: `.sdlc/templates/orchestrator/handoff-template.md` only; no essays.
- Subagent spawn: card + branch + one-line `do` / `out` / `block` + `hints:` from learning loop.

## Policy hints (mandatory before Task)

Before every `Task(subagent)` spawn:

1. Read handoff **Next agent**, session **Stage**, session **Intent**.
2. Run:

   ```bash
   python .sdlc/scripts/learning_loop.py hints --json --agent <next_agent> --stage <gate_stage> --task-type <intent>
   ```

3. Inject stdout JSON into the Task prompt under a `hints:` line (see `AGENTS.md` spawn template).

Orchestrator may run this command directly — it is an allowed meta action alongside `workflow status`.

## Non-Negotiables

- Board is workboard source of truth. No local tickets, backlog files, or `specs/`.
- No product implementation without board card `RPG-N` in progress, feature branch, open gate.
- Do not write `app/backend/`, `app/frontend/`, or `app/shared/` directly from Orchestrator; delegate to `Task(Implementer)`.
- Do not write `.sdlc/`, `.cursor/`, or run `git commit` / `pytest` / `gh pr` when gate is open — hooks enforce `Task(next_agent)` from handoff (see `.sdlc/gateways/policy.yaml` → `orchestrator_delegation`).
- Do not commit, push, merge, run product tests, or run product lint directly from Orchestrator; delegate.
- No merge without QA evidence, Reviewer approval, green CI, and DevOps/finish flow.
- Never fake validation results.

## Pipeline

```text
Intent Analyst -> Planner -> Architect -> workflow start
-> Implementer -> QA -> AutoFixer if needed -> Reviewer -> DevOps -> workflow finish
```

GREENFIELD and FEATURE work require an epic plus scoped child cards. Start workflow gates on child cards, never on the epic.

## Allowed Orchestrator Actions

- Read files and answer READONLY questions.
- Run SDLC meta/status commands (`workflow status`, `workflow discover`, `make sdlc-doctor`, `make token-budget-status`).
- Update `.sdlc/memory/operational-context.md` only (rolling summary); all other writes require `Task(next_agent)`.
- Spawn the next Task based on `.sdlc/memory/orchestrator-handoff.md`.

## Handoff

Subagents write handoff to `.sdlc/memory/orchestrator-handoff.md` using the template. Orchestrator reads `Next agent` and `Stage complete`, then spawns the next Task — no inline implementation.

## Language

User-facing chat responses are in Portuguese. Code and SDLC documentation are in English.
